It is Wednesday evening, and I am on my way home.
I stop at a small greengrocer.
There are also many special spices there.
I am cooking a big meal this weekend and need certain ingredients.
I find the small jars quickly on the shelf.
I take them with me to the till.
"Good evening," the shopkeeper says warmly.
"Good evening," I answer and put the spices on the counter.
He scans the jars unhurriedly.
"That makes four euros fifty-five, please," he says.
I pay with my card.
"Do you need the till receipt?" he asks me.
"No, thank you," I answer.
I open my backpack.
I pack the small jars safely into the backpack.
"Have a nice evening," the shopkeeper says.
"Thank you, to you too," I say goodbye.
Outside on the street it is still light and summery warm.
I walk the rest of the way comfortably.
A little later I reach the flat.
